  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When you decide to get a new backsplash, it's usually a pretty quick process compared to a full shower install, but there are still key steps involved to get that perfect finish. First, the pros will meticulously measure the wall space to figure out the best tile layout, making sure to minimize awkward cuts, especially around outlets and cabinets. Then, it's all about prep: ensuring the wall surface is clean, dry, and flat for optimal tile adhesion. Next, the thinset adhesive is applied to the wall, and the tiles are carefully set with consistent spacing, often using spacers to keep everything uniform. After the tiles are set and the thinset has dried, it's time for grouting. This fills the spaces between the tiles and really brings the whole look together. Finally, the edges are neatly finished, and any necessary caulking is applied where the backsplash meets the countertop or cabinets. While it's generally a faster project, proper drying times for grout and sealant are still important before the area is fully functional and ready for daily use. We at HH Remodeling LLC make sure every step is handled with care for a beautiful, lasting result."
    }
  ],
